Teaching Moshi
==============

This teaching project contains modified and independently reorganized code derived
from the following official projects:

* kyutai-labs/moshi (PyTorch implementation), Copyright (c) Kyutai,
  licensed under the MIT License. See LICENSES/MIT-moshi.txt.
* AudioCraft components used by the Moshi PyTorch implementation,
  Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates, licensed under the MIT
  License. See LICENSES/MIT-audiocraft.txt.
* kyutai-labs/moshi-finetune, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  See LICENSES/Apache-2.0-moshi-finetune.txt.

The modifications remove production-only concerns (distributed training, FSDP,
CUDA Graph capture, quantized deployment, server clients, and multiple backends),
add data-flow-oriented teaching interfaces, synthetic datasets, tests, semantic
distillation and training entry points, and reorganize the model configuration.
The official packages are not imported or required at runtime.

Original ai-whys code and modifications are covered by the repository's Apache
License 2.0; see LICENSE. Third-party components retain their original licenses.
Model weights, tokenizers, and datasets have separate terms which must be checked
before use or redistribution.
